AB  - Cutting carbon dioxide emissions isn't enough, according to the most recent report from the United Nations Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change . Society will need to claw back a lot of the CO 2 already in the atmosphere to avoid the worst effects of climate change. XPrize Carbon Removal is a $100 million technology contest that aims to help answer that call. The contest organizers have now narrowed down the initial crop of more than 1,300 entrants to 20 finalists . The companies in this final round are split almost evenly among four carbon removal methods: direct air capture, mineralization, biochar creation, and direct ocean removal . To qualify for the grand prize, the firms must deploy and operate pilot plants that capture CO 2 at a rate of 1,000 metric tons (t) per year or better. The judges will select the winner on the basis of the technology's potential
