AB  - Extensive research on carbon-related processes has focused primarily on seaweed aquaculture, leaving carbon dynamics within shrimp pond systems relatively underexplored. Dynamic changes in organic carbon in aquaculture sediments (June-September 2022, for a total of 85 days) were measured in Penaeus vannamei pond monoculture (P) and P. vannamei - Mercenaria mercenaria integrated pond culture (PM) systems. The effects of the main physicochemical factors of the water column and environmental exposure were analyzed. The refractory dissolved organic carbon (RDOC) content in surface sediments was monitored. The main results were as follows: (1) During the culture period, the total organic carbon (TOC) content of sediments ranged from 2.46 f 0.27 to 4.12 f 0.17 and 3.22 f 0.01 to 4.80 f 0.23 g center dot kg- 1dw, particulate organic carbon (POC) content ranged from 2.43 f 0.27 to 4.07 f 0.17 and 3.20 f 0.01 to 4.75 f 0.23 g center dot kg-1dw, dissolved organic carbon (DOC) content ranged from 26.80 f 0.34 to 43.07 f 0.15 and 26.81 f 0.14 to 55.09 f 1.05 mg center dot kg-1dw, RDOC content ranged from 5.27 f 0.23 to 25.11 f 0.22 and 5.44 f 0.19 to 24.46 f 0.16 mg center dot kg- 1dw, and RDOC/DOC ranged from 19.67 f 0.89 to 58.29 f 0.31 and 20.30 f 0.61 to 63.17 f 0.48% for P and PM systems, respectively. Farming activities significantly increased organic carbon contents of sediments, with the sedimentary organic carbon being significantly higher in the PM system than in the P system at the end of the cultivation period; (2) organic carbon contents of sediments of the two culture systems showed significant positive correlations with water alkalinity, chlorophyll-a, nitrate nitrogen, and reactive phosphate; (3) environmental sunlight exposure significantly reduced the organic carbon contents of sediments in both P and PM systems, reducing the average TOC content by 12.18% and 11.75%, POC by 12.29% and 11.86%, DOC by 5.80% and 5.88%, RDOC by 28.63% and 32.76%, and RDOC/DOC by 23.42% and 28.90%, respectively. Based on the above data, it was calculated that average RDOC of 18.38 kg.ha- 1 and 21.24 kg.ha- 1 were present in the top 5 cm of surface sediment during the culture period in P and PM systems, respectively. The results provide empirical support for the assessment of carbon sequestration effects of P. vannamei marine pond aquaculture systems.
