KW  - NUTRIENT
KW  - SEA
AB  - A fundamental issue in marine science is the identification of the factors controlling biological uptake of CO2 in high nitrate, low-chlorophyll regions(1-10). A recent in situ iron fertilization experiment demonstrated that iron limitation is responsible for low phytoplankton stocks in the equatorial Pacific(4), Here we show that flavodoxin, a biochemical marker of iron limitation, can be used to map the degree of iron stress in natural populations. Flavodoxin assays along a 900-km east-west transect in the northeastern subarctic Pacific revealed a pronounced increase in iron stress in the region west of the 135 degrees W meridian. Addition of dissolved iron alleviated this stress. Immunostaining of single cells from the most western station showed that flavodoxin is present specifically within the chloroplasts of diatoms. Our approach provides a rapid means of defining the extent of iron stress in the ocean(5) and supports the hypothesis that diatoms are iron stressed in the northeast Pacific(6,10).
