AB  - Ocean iron fertilization is a new process many companies are planning to develop in order to control atmospheric carbon dioxide. Iron is essential for the growth of phytoplanktons and iron fertilization depends on whether the carbon stays sunk in the deep ocean. Phytoplanktons fix 50 billion tons of carbon per year and naturally grow when iron-containing dust drifts into ocean waters. Hence, companies like Planktos are planning to spread tons of iron over the ocean with the aim of triggering oversized blooms of phytoplankton.
